From af4a4b1f63911ed1a39c326711ea5a5a7da95c32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emily Astranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:08:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: add contrast autofocus

Port of the OnePlus 7T Pro bringup's contrast autofocus for the software
ISP onto libcamera 0.8.0, where the IPA lives in src/ipa/softisp and the
exposure loop comes from libipa.

The CPU statistics gain an exposure-normalized horizontal green edge
energy. The IPA receives the lens control map at configure time and
returns a focus position with every stats result; the simple pipeline
applies it to the sensor's focus lens straight away, outside the delayed
sensor controls. The Af algorithm waits until the AGC has requested the
same exposure and gain for three stats frames, runs a coarse-to-fine scan
over the actuator range, parks at the sharpest position, and in
continuous mode rescans when the sharpness at the locked position falls
to 65 %. AfMode, AfTrigger, AfState and a normalized LensPosition are
exposed. Scan steps are a quarter and a twentieth of the range, a lock is
held for 15 stats frames before continuous mode may rescan, and a scan
starts after 12 stats frames even if the exposure loop never settles.

